# Cell from playpick: mode=menus, view=1280x800, save=fresh.
#
# Every mode=menus session so far (2026-09-25-9, -19, -30, 2026-09-26-1,
# -10, -24, -34) used --profile playtest/profile, i.e. save=carried -- but
# #273 already established that a carried run only ever sees its own
# invocation's port, so every one of those sessions actually played a fresh
# origin without the ledger ever saying so explicitly. This is the first
# menus session to be honestly labelled fresh (no --profile at all) and the
# first on a desktop/mouse viewport with no prior carried-desktop baggage
# (2026-09-26-10/-34 were both carried at this same 1280x800). Surveying
# the front page's own share line (README: "a player who has done nothing
# yet claims nothing"), the raid setup screen's lock state, and the record
# screen's zero-state, on a save that is actually, unambiguously new.

open
targets
ui
shot front

tap share
shot front-shared
targets

open
tap raid
targets
ui
shot raid-setup

tap difficulty
shot difficulty-open
targets

key Escape
tap next
targets
shot classpick

tap back
tap back
open
tap settings
targets
ui
shot settings

tap name
shot name-focused
targets

tap back
open
tap record
targets
ui
shot record

tap back
open
